{
  "behaviorChanges": [
    "New verb `tautline merge [pr]`: reads the PR's live statusCheckRollup, refuses when a check FAILED (or, with blockOnPending, has not reported yet), then merges via gh. The PR is an explicit ARGUMENT or the current branch's PR -- never parsed out of a command string.",
    "New optional adapter key `mergeGate` {enforcement: off|advise|block, blockOnPending}, absent-safe and defaulting to `advise`.",
    "Target-changing gh flags (--repo/-R/--admin, every spelling) are REFUSED rather than forwarded: forwarded, they let the gate verify one PR and merge another. A PR URL also reveals its own repo, so the cross-repo fail-closed rule fires for URL targets.",
    "The verified head commit is pinned via --match-head-commit, so a push landing between verification and merge cannot be merged on the old commit's checks.",
    "Fail-OPEN with an explicit notice for a SAME-repo unverifiable verdict; cross-repo fails CLOSED. Routine --admin stays forbidden; --override records a hard-to-reverse decision BEFORE the merge.",
    "Two kernel defects deferred from 0.34.0 are fixed here, where the code first becomes reachable: pending now outranks unknown in BOTH modes, and wrapper flags taking non-numeric operands no longer hide a wrapped raw merge.",
    "The `--` separator is consumed rather than forwarded to gh, which would otherwise stop option parsing and read the forwarded flags as positionals. A no-value wrapper flag (env/sudo `-i`) no longer swallows `gh` itself, and the strip refuses to consume the command head whatever the flag list says."
  ],
